🎓 Learning Outcomes & Interview Talking Points
If you are reviewing this project (or if I am interviewing with you), here are the key engineering concepts demonstrated:

Compiler Construction: Implementing Lexers, Parsers, ASTs, and Semantic Analysis from scratch without relying on heavy external libraries.

Graph Optimization: Understanding Directed Acyclic Graphs (DAGs), topological sorting, dead code elimination, and common subexpression elimination (CSE).

Multi-Provider Abstraction: Designing clean interfaces (Adapter Pattern) to switch between different AI APIs seamlessly.

Real-time Distributed Systems: Using WebSockets to stream execution events and handle asynchronous state updates in React.

Full-Stack Architecture: Integrating a Python backend, a React frontend, and an SQLite database into a cohesive, responsive application.

UI/UX Design: Building complex interactive interfaces like drag-and-drop graphs (React Flow) and code editors (Monaco) with a premium aesthetic.

🗺️ Future Roadmap
While this is a practice project, future iterations could include:

□ Local LLM Support: Integrate Ollama to run models like Llama 3 locally (requires GPU).
□ Advanced Optimizer Passes: Add loop unrolling and branch prediction for conditionals.
□ Workflow Versioning: Track changes to workflows over time and allow rollbacks.
□ Cost Control: Set hard limits on token usage per execution to prevent runaway costs.
□ Dockerization: Provide a docker-compose.yml for one-click deployment.
⚠️ Disclaimer
This project is built purely for educational and portfolio purposes. It is explicitly not production-ready. It is designed to run on a CPU-only laptop and relies on cloud APIs for LLM inference. Do not use this for enterprise-level workloads. Keep your .env files secret and never commit API keys.

📄 License
This project is licensed under the MIT License. See the LICENSE file for details.

🙏 Acknowledgements
The Dragon Book (Compilers: Principles, Techniques, and Tools) for the foundational concepts.

FastAPI and React teams for incredible developer experiences.

React Flow for making graph UI development so easy.

Google Gemini for providing free API access for learners.

Built with ☕, 🧠, and a deep love for compilers and AI.

