### 🚀 Final Step: GitHub Par Upload Karne Ka Command

Dono parts ko ek `README.md` file mein save karne ke baad, apne terminal mein ye commands run kar:

```bash
git add README.md
git commit -m "Added highly detailed README documentation with full architecture and schemas"
git push origin main
Ab tu apna GitHub repo khol ke dekh, ekdum Zero to Hero level ka professional project lagega! Agar aage koi error aaye toh batana. 🚀

giginore file
Bhai, GitHub par jab bhi koi naya repo banate hain, toh ek .gitignore file zaroor banani chahiye. Ye file Git ko batati hai ki kaunsi files GitHub par upload nahi karni hain (jaise API keys, virtual environment, ya node_modules).

Agar tu ye file nahi banayega, toh tera project bohot bada aur ganda dikhega, aur sabse bada khatra—tera Gemini API key leak ho jayega.

Ye lo ekdum perfect aur professional .gitignore file. Is code ko copy karke apne project folder (jahan README.md hai wahi) mein .gitignore naam se save kar de (dhyan rakhna, file ke aage dot . zaroor hai).

